<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> The human being was created in God's image, wounded by original sin, yet God never abandoned us and promised redemption from the very beginning.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that the human being is God's image, created for communion.</li>
<li>Know the unity of body and soul as an essential part of human dignity.</li>
<li>Understand original sin: not mere disobedience, but pride and distrust in God.</li>
<li>Recognize the consequences of sin: the wounded nature, concupiscence, broken relationships.</li>
<li>Embrace the promise of the Protoevangelium: where sin increased, grace abounded all the more.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;Where sin increased, grace abounded all the more&raquo; (Rom 5:20)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 355-421</p>

</section>

